abstract: >
  AegisVision is a distributed, autonomous, GPU-native visual-intelligence
  operating system for realtime multimodal perception, reasoning, and
  orchestration at planetary scale. It is composed of 35 Go services,
  14 shared libraries, 38 Helm charts, 30 Architecture Decision Records,
  and a complete set of compliance evidence packages (SOC 2, EU AI Act,
  GDPR DPIA, pen-test scope). The platform implements bounded-autonomy
  agentic AI, Wilson lower-bound canary promotion, same-URN shadow
  inference, multi-window burn-rate SLOs, JS/KL/TVD drift detection,
  predictive prefetch via a 7×24 EMA grid, and a signed air-gapped
  install bundle as a day-one CI artifact.
